// Project: occupant behavior in BIM-to-BEM workflows. Source: Chung et al., Building Simulation 2025 (md copy).
//   BIM, gbXML v7.04            4.2: "validates the input gbXML file against the latest version of gbXML v7.04 schema";
//                                3.2: "reuses BIM models from gbXML files"
//   gb-obXML converter          3.2 and 4.2; the three nodes on the spine are the three steps of Fig. 6 (validate gbXML,
//                                mapping rules, validate obXML)
//   OBXML V1.4                  abstract: "The enhanced obXML schema v1.4"
//   spaces, systems, schedules  3.2: "focusing on spatial elements, building systems, and operational schedules"
//   behavior models             abstract: "documentation of a window operation behavior model" (the window and curve)
//   SIMULATION, BIM-to-BEM      abstract: "within the BIM-to-BEM simulation workflows"; dashed because 6.2: "current OB
//   workflows                    tools like obFMU and OB Model Library use obXML v1.3.3"
// Illustrative, not from the sources: the plan of spaces and the energy model massing. No occupants are drawn: this is
// a schema and converter study, not human subjects work.
// Style C, exploded axonometric (approved style sheet, diagram-styles.html), sized for the project card:
// the drawing group is scaled, the labels are not. Classes: .dgc in global.css.
---
